<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  memqd — the resident index behind the UserPromptSubmit hook.

  This file is the source of truth; the live copy is at
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.108.memqd.plist. Do not copy it by hand —
  `scripts/install.sh` writes it, substituting $HOME and the install prefix,
  and restarts the agent. Paths below are absolute because launchd expands
  neither ~ nor $HOME.

  The binary lives in ~/.local/bin, NOT in target/release. It used to live in
  target/, and a disk cleanup that removed target/ took the MCP server, the
  UserPromptSubmit hook and this daemon down together (2026-08-29).

  Why an agent at all: before this, the daemon was started by hand. It did not
  survive a reboot, and `memq hook`'s fallback only spawns a replacement on the
  *next* prompt — so the first prompt after every restart silently got no
  memory. That is the exact failure the hook was built to remove.

  KeepAlive restarts it if it dies or is killed. It does NOT need a file
  watcher: the daemon re-stats the store on each request and reindexes itself
  when a memory changes (see store_stamp() in src/lib.rs).

  So a request is not always just a search. If a reindex is in flight, the
  daemon drives it for up to FRESHNESS_GRACE (3 s) before answering, so that a
  memory written a moment ago is searchable now. A query that blocks for a
  couple of seconds right after a write is that, not a hang.

-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.108.memqd</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/yongyutjantaboot/.local/bin/memq</string>
        <string>serve</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Index build is ~2.6 s; without a throttle a crash-loop would spin the
         CPU rebuilding embeddings. 30 s is long enough to notice in the log. -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>30</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/yongyutjantaboot/Library/Logs/memqd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/yongyutjantaboot/Library/Logs/memqd.log</string>

    <!-- memqd reads nothing relative to cwd (store and cache paths are built
         from $HOME), so this deliberately does not point at the checkout: the
         daemon must not stop booting because the repo moved. -->
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/yongyutjantaboot</string>
</dict>
</plist>
